<p>Liposuction in Delhi is a surgical procedure that removes fat by sucking out excess fat through a hollow thin metal rod(cannula) which is attached to a vacuum pump. It is considered the most common, best, and safest fat reduction method. It is useful to reduce fat from specific areas such as the abdomen, thighs, arms, chin, back, buttocks, neck, etc., and for body contouring. It is mostly done under general anesthesia.</p>
<p>It is not a weight loss alternative and not an obesity treatment. Through this article, we will give a basic understanding of liposuction, such as who needs it, and where you can consult for the best liposuction surgery in Delhi.</p>

<h2 id="list_1" class="blog_heading">Symptoms</h2>

<p>Liposuction surgery in Delhi can be considered as an option if you have below listed symptoms:</p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1">You are unable to lose stubborn fat; however, you should be within 30% of your ideal weight with no history of massive weight loss.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Treatment of breast reduction or gynecomastia.</li>
<li aria-level="1">You do not have any underlying medical conditions.</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Diagnoses</strong></h2>
<p>Liposuction surgery in Delhi is a confirmed diagnosis for individuals with excess fat and stubborn pockets having flat abdominal walls and good skin tone. When a healthy diet and continuous exercise fails to get rid of the body fat bulges, liposuction (also known as lipo, lipoplasty, liposculpture suction, or lipectomy) is a good option to achieve the desired body contour. A good candidate having stable body weight overall but excess fat in specific spots of the body can also be diagnosed.</p>
<h2><strong>Treatment</strong></h2>
<p>Liposuction surgery in Delhi is also used to treat gynecomastia or breast reduction along with removing fat from the desired areas of the body such as the abdomen, hip, thighs, arms, ankles, buttocks, mons pubis, facial features including face, neck, and chin. However, one must remember that liposuction is not considered as a typical treatment of overall alternative of weight loss. Having unrealistic expectations for the surgery might impact the thought process of the patient leading to labeling it as unsuccessful liposuction. Thus, it is imperative to understand the complete treatment and after-care instructions to help in achieving the desired results.</p>

<h2><strong>What are the 3 types of liposuction?</strong></h2>
<p>The types of liposuction are categorised based on the technique used to remove the extra fat tissues. The three major types of liposuction are:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Tumescent liposuction or fluid injection:</strong> One of the most commonly performed types of liposuction, tumescent liposuction or fluid injection, involves injecting injections with the medicated solution into the fat removal areas. The injected sites get numb, and the fluid and the fat are suctioned out slowly.</li>
    <li><strong>Ultrasound-assisted liposuction (UAL):</strong> UAL utilises ultrasound waves to transform the fat cells into a fluid. After which, the fluid cells are vacuumed or drained out. This technique removes the dense fibrous fat from the upper back and enlarged male breast tissues. Sometimes, UAL with tumescent liposuction type gives better outcomes and precise results.</li>
    <li><strong>Laser-assisted liposuction (LAL):</strong>LAL type of liposuction uses laser energy to fluidify the fat cells that are later vacuumed out or drained out through small tubes. The small tubes in LAL help drain fat easily from smaller regions of the body such as the chin, jawline, and face. The lasers used in LAL stimulate collagen generation that helps prevent the sagging of skin post-liposuction.</li>
</ul>

<h2><strong>Which liposuction is best?</strong></h2>
<p>The surgeon decides the type or technique of liposuction depending on the area of liposuction. While UAL helps suck out fat from the dense fibrous regions of the body, LAL helps remove fat from the small sections of the body. However, the most common and popular type of liposuction is <strong>tumescent liposuction</strong>. Generally, performed as an outpatient procedure without anaesthesia, tumescent, or fluid injection is the most effective, safer, and less painful type of liposuction with a quicker recovery time. </p>


<h2><strong>Is liposuction available in India?</strong></h2>
<p>Liposuction, the cosmetic surgical procedure, is of great aesthetic value in India. Many cosmetic surgeons in India commonly perform liposuction. Statistical data from the Association of Plastic Surgeons of India [APSI] database-2013 indicates an average number of 32.5 liposuction surgeries per year. And the number of liposuction has been increasing year on year. </p>

<h2><strong>How many kg can liposuction remove?</strong></h2>
<p>The amount of fat that can be removed through liposuction differs on the targeted area of liposuction. However, the average amount of fat vacuumed out during liposuction ranges from 0.9kgs to 1.25kgs. In general, 30% of your fat accumulated in localised pockets is eliminated.</p>

