<h2><strong>How much does arm liposuction cost in India?</h2></strong>
<p>As mentioned earlier, the area of fat removal determines the cost of liposuction. The cost of arm liposuction in India ranges between 50,000 to 1,00,000 depending on the technique, clinic, surgeon, and other cost-deciding factors. </p>

<h2><strong>Different Techniques for Liposuction In Delhi</strong></h2>
<p>Different types of liposuction surgery are listed below:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Fluid injection or Tumescent liposuction</strong> is the most common type of liposuction in delhi that involves injecting with a large volume of the medicated solution of anesthesia, epinephrine, and salt solution into the areas before fat removal. Depending on the requirement and patient&rsquo;s goal, the volume can be up to three times the amount of fat needed to be removed.</li>
<li>The <strong>super-wet technique</strong> is similar to the fluid injection; however, the difference lies in the amount of fluid to be injected which is equal to the fat amount to be removed in this scenario. This technique comparatively consumes less time to operate; however, requires general anesthesia or sedation.</li>
<li><strong>Ultrasound-assisted liposuction (UAL)</strong> is the process of removing fat by ultrasonic vibrations followed by vacuuming the fat cells. It is chosen to be performed in two different ways: external where above the skin surface is operated; or internal where below the skin surface is operated by heated cannula. In some of the follow-up procedures of UAL, it can be combined with fluid injection techniques for enhanced precision.</li>
<li><strong>Laser-assisted liposuction (LAL)</strong> involves a laser technique to liquefy the fat cells that allows them to be vacuumed or drained out via small tubes. Surgeons prefer using LAL for smaller areas to be covered such as jowls, face, and chin because cannula used during LAL are comparatively smaller in size than used in other techniques of liposuction in delhi. However, an advantage of LAL includes collagen production from laser energy which helps in preventing sagging of the skin post-procedure.</li>
</ol>
<h2><strong>Procedure (Pre, During &amp; After)</strong></h2>
<p>The steps of the liposuction procedure include anesthesia, incision, and observing results.</p>
<p>&nbsp;<strong>Before the surgery</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Fasting for at least 6 hours is required. Do not eat, drink, or chew during this period.</li>
<li>Stop taking all medications including hormonal supplements, aspirin, and herbal medicines at least 10 days before the surgery date.</li>
<li>Surgical areas need to be washed properly with antibacterial starting 3 days before the surgery date.</li>
<li>Avoid smoking at least 4 weeks before and avoid drinking at least 2 days before the surgery date.</li>
<li>Start taking Vitamin-C supplements starting from two weeks before the surgery date to facilitate immune system stabilization and faster healing post-surgery.</li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;<strong>During the surgery</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Equipment such as a cannula and liposuction machine used is sterilized.</li>
<li>The surgical area to be treated is sterilized and prepared for incision.</li>
<li>General or local anesthesia will be provided depending on the patient&rsquo;s profile.</li>
<li>A small incision is made on the skin, and the fluid is injected under the skin in the area to be covered.</li>
<li>Once the medicated solution starts taking effect, the fat initiates to dislodge which is vacuumed via a suction tube or a large syringe.</li>
<li>The surgeon might puncture several skin areas as required by an individual patient to achieve the best contour.</li>
<li>Once the fat is vacuumed and removed, small drainage tubes are inserted into the defatted areas to remove fluid and blood that is required to collect during the initial few days after the surgery. If in case you observed the fluid loss at a higher pace, inform your surgeon to substitute the drainage tube with intravenous fluid replacement.</li>
<li>A compression garment will be recommended to wear to avoid any abrasion.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>After the surgery:</strong></p>
<p>Once the procedure is completed, mild discomfort along with redness, swelling, and bruising is observed. Prescribed medications will assist in taking care of the pain and minimizing the risk of any infection. Incisions will stay open for a while and temporary drains will be placed to promote excess fluid drainage. It is suggested to wear tight compression garments for the initial few weeks which will assist in reducing swelling. Avoid any strenuous activities or going to work for a few weeks and give proper care to your body for optimum healing. Some contour irregularities may also be observed during this time as the remaining fat in the body starts to settle into positions.</p>
<p>You will not observe the results right after the liposuction surgery, however, swelling or fluid retention in the treated area might make you feel a gained weight and bloated. As the swelling will subside upon proper care, you will begin to see the results. Loose skin will also be observed which will become firm over time. Any additional surgical intervention might also be necessary for skin tightening around the treated area depending on the patient&rsquo;s profile of age or amount of fat removed. Depending on the number of treated areas and amount of fat removed, final results will be expected to observe between 1-3 months of the liposuction surgery in Delhi.</p>
<h2><strong>Post Operative Care</strong></h2>
<p>Aftercare of the surgery is crucial to ensure faster recovery and healing.</p>
<ol>
<li>Your body requires quiet rest immediately after liposuction in delhi and the effect of anesthesia stays for 2-3 days and hence it is suggested to avoid any driving or motor activities.</li>
<li>It is advisable to change the dressing of the incisions every day as you might observe blood or fluid oozing out.</li>
<li>It is imperative to take short walks every 1-2 hours in your home until your bedtime to prevent any clots.</li>
<li>Prescribed medications for pain and swelling need to be followed as per schedule.</li>
<li>Avoid smoking and alcohol consumption during the recovery phase.</li>
<li>Wear loose garments in post-operative care duration to ensure no irritation and rashes appear at the incision sites which may hinder the healing process.</li>
<li>If you are unable to urinate or do not feel the urge to urinate after 8 hours of surgery, please seek immediate medical attention.</li>
<li>Consult your surgeon with follow-up visits to ensure proper healing.</li>
</ol>
<p>Swelling will start to subside within a few weeks and you will observe less bulkiness in the treated area. The observation will be a leaner appearance in the upcoming several months. Although liposuction surgery in delhi removes a certain amount of fat cells in the treated area, the remaining fat cells will continue to grow in size by storing fat. Inculcating a balanced diet along with plenty of water and fluids in your routine would be of importance as fat distribution will change if you start gaining weight after liposuction. It will facilitate healing and maintain a healthy basal metabolic rate (BMR) and body weight which will help you in achieving the desired body contour once the swelling subsides completely.</p>

<h2 id="list_1" class="blog_heading">Who needs it and who is the ideal candidate for liposuction?</h2>


<p>Always consult a good cosmetic or plastic surgeon to discuss your needs and requirements. We at Iconique can assure you the best liposuction surgery in Delhi. Get yourself assessed and know the best treatment option for you and whether you are the right candidate for liposuction. Also, you must understand that liposuction does not treat stretch marks and skin irregularities. You are a good candidate for liposuction if:</p>
<ol>
<li aria-level="1">If you wish to improve your appearance and get rid of localized stubborn fat depositions in certain areas of your body.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If lifestyle changes have not helped you achieve the desired results and the fat depositions do not go by regular exercise and a balanced diet.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you have otherwise a stable body weight.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you have a good skin tone and elasticity and the skin can easily mold into new contours.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you are over 18 years of age.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you have overall good health.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you are not suffering from blood flow problems like coronary artery disease and other diseases like diabetes.</li>
<li aria-level="1">You have good immunity.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you do not smoke or have stopped smoking.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Are dedicated to maintaining your body weight with a healthy diet and regular exercise.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Have expectations that are realistic of the results of the procedure.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>You must not go for liposuction if:</b></p>
<ol>
<li aria-level="1">You are pregnant or nursing.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you are taking blood-thinning medications and cannot discontinue them for even a few weeks.</li>
<li aria-level="1">If you are allergic to lidocaine which is the anesthesia used for the procedure.</li>
</ol>

